Tiny GPT notes

Current state
- Parser now removes attachment/system spam like `You sent an attachment.`
- Media-only and link-only share messages are dropped from training text.
- Share text is kept when it contains real text.
- Word-level tokenization is now the default.
- Corpus building now merges short fragmented chat lines into longer sentence-like spans.
- Optional `--clean-training-text` mode drops mojibake-heavy and junky lines.

Important reality
- This is still a small from-scratch GPT.
- Better output depends more on data quality than GPU.
- If the corpus is noisy, the model will learn noisy text.
- If the corpus is tiny, the model will repeat or collapse.

Recommended workflow

1. Build a cleaner corpus
```bash
PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python scripts/prepare_data.py \
  --input-dir "fuck" \
  --clean-training-text \
  --output-text "data/processed/all_cleaner.txt" \
  --output-jsonl "data/processed/all_cleaner.jsonl"
```

2. Train with the word tokenizer
```bash
PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python scripts/train.py \
  --input-text "data/processed/all_cleaner.txt" \
  --run-name "all-word-cleaner" \
  --tokenizer-type word \
  --context-length 32 \
  --embedding-dim 64 \
  --num-heads 4 \
  --num-layers 2 \
  --batch-size 8 \
  --max-steps 800 \
  --train-split 0.9 \
  --eval-interval 50 \
  --eval-batches 4 \
  --learning-rate 1e-4 \
  --device cuda
```

3. Generate text
```bash
PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python scripts/generate.py \
  --checkpoint "artifacts/all-word-cleaner/best.pt" \
  --prompt "can i say something " \
  --max-new-tokens 60 \
  --temperature 0.8 \
  --top-k 10 \
  --repetition-penalty 1.25 \
  --only-new-text \
  --device cuda
```

What changed in code
- `src/tinygpt/instagram_parser.py`
  - safer file reading with replacement for bad bytes
  - text sanitization for invisible/control junk
  - better filtering of attachment/system noise
  - sentence-like merging of short fragmented messages
  - optional training-clean filtering

- `src/tinygpt/tokenizer.py`
  - default tokenizer is word-level
  - character tokenizer still available
  - checkpoint loading supports both tokenizer types

- `scripts/train.py`
  - supports `--tokenizer-type`

- `scripts/generate.py`
  - supports temperature/top-k/repetition penalty/greedy/only-new-text

Known limitations
- Some mojibake can still survive in the dataset.
- Hindi/Indic text is not handled as well as a real subword tokenizer would handle it.
- This project can improve further, but it will not behave like a large pretrained LLM.

Likely next improvements
- stronger English-clean mode
- real subword tokenizer
- better sentence-end stopping during generation
- more training text from the same writing style
